## What this does not cover

**Source texts are not licensed by this repository, because this repository does
not distribute them.**

The manifests carry pointers, spans, licences and SHA-256 hashes. The texts
themselves are fetched by whoever runs a cycle, from the sources named in the
manifests, and are git-ignored. Each remains under its own licence — CC BY,
CC BY-SA, public domain, or a research-use release — and those terms are what
govern your use of it.

If you redistribute anything you build on this benchmark, attribute the source
corpora as their own licences require. Where a manifest entry names a corpus with
a citation (FCE, Blog Authorship, WritingPrompts, Europarl), cite the original
paper.

## Attribution

